# Project-local override of the ClaudeKit ignore baseline.
#
# The shipped baseline blocks directory-name patterns so that large build output
# directories cannot fill LLM context. The hook matches those words anywhere in a
# Bash command, not just in paths, which blocks ordinary Go development here:
#
#   build  - `go build` is the standard compile command
#   target - a common Go identifier (and this repo has no Rust/Java target/ dir)
#
# This project is Go and has neither a build/ nor a target/ directory, so allowing
# both is safe here without weakening the baseline for JS/TS or Rust projects.
!build
!target
